# Lines starting with '#' will be removed
# This template wraps the review replies sent from the b4 review
# TUI (both per-patch replies and the cover-letter reply). Point
# b4.review-reply-template at this file in your git config to
# enable it:
# [b4]
#   review-reply-template = ~/.config/b4/review-reply-template
#
# The template MUST contain the ${reply} placeholder -- it expands
# to the reply content itself: the quoted patch context, your
# comments and any trailers. A template without ${reply} is ignored.
#
# Other available placeholders:
#   ${fromname}  - sender's full name (e.g. "Jane Developer")
#   ${firstname} - first word of the sender's name (e.g. "Jane")
#   ${fromemail} - sender's email address
#   ${subject}   - subject of the message being replied to
#   ${sentdate}  - date of the message being replied to
#   ${msgid}     - message-id of the message being replied to
#   ${myname}    - your own name
#   ${myemail}   - your own email address
#   ${signature} - your email signature (~/.signature if present)
#
# If the rendered reply does not already contain a signature
# delimiter ("-- " on its own line), your signature is appended
# automatically, so most templates do not need ${signature}.
Hi ${firstname},

${reply}

Cheers,
${myname}
